AB  - In this study, image datasets of cocoa leaves and pods, both from local cocoa farms in Uganda, specifically in a place called Bundibugyo were supplemented with more cocoa image datasets from Kaggle and were used in training multiple deep learning models for comparison and development of a mobile based cocoa plant disease detection system. The models developed were evaluated and compared using prediction accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score. Experimental results show that the MobileNetV2 model performed best and was deployed in the cocoa disease detection mobile application, with a test accuracy of 0.9965, a test loss of 0.0203, a precision of 0.9965, a recall of 0.9965, an F1 Score of 0.9965, and an AUC score of 1.0000.
